---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="256x256" href="/favicon-original-tent-close.png?v=7" />
		<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png?v=7" />
		<title>About — Olivia Fjord Sloth</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Meet Olivia Fjord Sloth: physicist, adventurer, speaker and long-distance hiker." />
	</head>

	<body>

		<SiteHeader />


		<main>

			<!-- INTRO -->

			<section class="intro">

				<div class="intro-text">
					<p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE ABOUT ME</p>

					<h1>Hi, I’m Olivia.</h1>

					<p class="lead">
                        I have a PhD in physics, and I think the researcher in me has followed
                        me into the way I travel. I ask a lot of questions. I don’t always find
                        particularly good answers, but I usually come home questioning something
                        I thought I knew before I left.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="intro-image">
					<img src="/tur2.webp" alt="Olivia Fjord Sloth in the mountains" decoding="async" />
				</div>

			</section>

            <!-- STORY -->

            <section class="story">

                <p class="eyebrow">HOW THIS STARTED</p>

                <div class="story-text">

                    <p>
                        My name is Olivia, and I’m an adventurer. It took me quite a long
                        time to realise that.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        For years, I didn’t really understand what kept pulling me towards
                        things that were difficult, unknown or maybe a little unlikely.
                        I’m dyslexic and somehow ended up with a PhD in physics. I’ve trained
                        for competitions, climbed mountains and travelled to places I knew
                        very little about.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        People have told me a lot of things I couldn’t do. I’ve always wanted
                        to find out for myself. My first thought is usually: <em>Why not?</em>
                        Sometimes followed by: <em>Watch me.</em>
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Finishing my PhD was probably harder for me than climbing Mount Everest.
                        And when I finally finished, I remember thinking:
                        <em>And then what?</em>
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        For a long time, I thought this was something I would grow out of.
                        You have your adventures, your gap year, your big trips — and then
                        you come home and start your “real” life.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Finding the word <em>adventurer</em> gave me a strange kind of calm.
                        It could hold all of it. And maybe I didn’t have to grow out of it
                        after all.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </section>


            <!-- WALKING -->

            <section class="story">

                <p class="eyebrow">WHY I WALK</p>

                <div class="story-text">

                    <p>
                        Walking is probably where I feel most at home in all of this.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        I’ve walked alone through the mountains of Kyrgyzstan and Tajikistan,
                        climbed Iran’s highest mountain, 5,610 metres, alone, and hiked and
                        travelled through Iraqi Kurdistan, Lebanon and Syria.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        There is something about moving through a country using only my own
                        body. I’m slow and vulnerable, and I can only carry what fits in my
                        backpack. I don’t go looking for anything in particular. I just walk.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        And somehow, walking makes some of the differences between people
                        feel less important.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        On Damavand in Iran, a woman once told me to take off my headscarf.
                        <em>“Up here, we are all free.”</em>
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        That stayed with me.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </section>


            <!-- QUESTIONS -->

            <section class="story">

                <p class="eyebrow">THINGS I KEEP WONDERING ABOUT</p>

                <div class="story-text">

                    <p>
                        I often come home with more questions than answers. If anything,
                        travelling makes me more curious — about the politics of the places
                        I visit, about people, but also about myself and the ethics of what I do.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        What risks am I willing to take? What is my role when I enter someone
                        else’s home, community or country? When am I curious, and when am I
                        crossing a line?
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        The people I meet stop being numbers in a headline. They become people
                        I know. People I care about. There is something beautiful about that,
                        but also something difficult.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        I’m not a journalist. I’m “just” a hiker. I’m the guest, and that
                        matters to me. I don’t want to arrive somewhere and decide what the
                        story is. I want to see what people want to show me and try to
                        understand what they want me to understand.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        I don’t always know what to do with that afterwards. And maybe that
                        is why I keep coming home with more questions.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </section>

			<!-- FACTS -->
            <section class="facts">

                <p class="eyebrow">A FEW ODD DETAILS</p>

                <div class="fact-grid">

                    <div class="fact">
                        <span>01</span>
                        <p>Once voted Denmark’s best female longboarder</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="fact">
                        <span>02</span>
                        <p>I’m still proud of discovering that you can dehydrate hummus</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="fact">
                        <span>03</span>
                        <p>Coffee can genuinely change my mood</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="fact">
                        <span>04</span>
                        <p>My ideal bedtime is 9 pm</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="fact">
                        <span>05</span>
                        <p>After a long hike, all I want is carrots and watermelon</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="fact">
                        <span>06</span>
                        <p>I swim in the sea all year round</p>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </section>


			<!-- CONTACT -->

			<section class="contact">

				<p class="eyebrow">COME SAY HI</p>

				<h2>
					Want to work together, book a talk or just say hi?
				</h2>

				<a class="contact-link" href="mailto:oliviasloth@hotmail.com">
					Get in touch →
				</a>

			</section>

		</main>

		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>


<style>

	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	html,
	body {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		background: #f4f1ea;
		color: #171717;
	}

	body {
		font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
	}

	a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: none;
	}


	/* HEADER */

	header {
		padding: 30px 48px;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.name {
		font-size: 22px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
	}

	nav {
		display: flex;
		gap: 32px;
	}

	nav a {
		font-size: 15px;
	}

	nav .active {
		border-bottom: 1px solid #171717;
	}


	/* INTRO */

    .intro {
        max-width: 1400px;
        margin: 70px auto 100px;
        padding: 0 48px;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.8fr;
		gap: 90px;
		align-items: center;
	}

    .eyebrow {
        margin: 0 0 20px;
        font-size: 11px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    }
    .story .eyebrow {
        max-width: 720px;
        margin: 0 0 20px auto;
    }
	h1 {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(60px, 7vw, 105px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 0.92;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}

	.lead {
		max-width: 720px;
		margin: 45px 0 0;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(25px, 2.4vw, 34px);
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: #555;
	}

	.intro-image img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
		object-fit: cover;
	}


	/* STORY */

	.story {
		max-width: 1000px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 48px 90px;
	}

	.story-text {
		max-width: 720px;
		margin-left: auto;
	}

	.story-text p {
		margin: 0 0 32px;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 22px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}


	/* FACTS */

	.facts {
		max-width: 1400px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 80px 48px 120px;
		border-top: 1px solid #b9b3a9;
	}

	.fact-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		margin-top: 50px;
	}

	.fact {
		padding: 35px 0;
		border-top: 1px solid #c8c2b8;

		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.fact:nth-child(odd) {
		padding-right: 50px;
	}

	.fact:nth-child(even) {
		padding-left: 50px;
	}

	.fact span {
		font-size: 12px;
		color: #777;
	}

	.fact p {
		margin: 0;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(24px, 2.2vw, 34px);
		line-height: 1.2;
	}


	/* CONTACT */

	.contact {
		max-width: 1000px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 100px 48px 140px;
	}

	.contact h2 {
		max-width: 800px;
		margin: 0 0 40px;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(42px, 5vw, 72px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.05;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
	}

	.contact-link {
		display: inline-block;
		font-weight: 700;
		border-bottom: 1px solid #171717;
		padding-bottom: 4px;
	}


	/* MOBILE */

	@media (max-width: 800px) {

		header {
			padding: 24px 20px;
		}

		.name {
			font-size: 17px;
		}

		nav {
			gap: 14px;
		}

		nav a {
			font-size: 13px;
		}


		.intro {
			margin: 60px auto 100px;
			padding: 0 24px;

			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 50px;
		}

		h1 {
			font-size: 64px;
		}

		.lead {
			font-size: 24px;
		}

		.intro-image {
			order: -1;
		}


		.story {
			padding: 0 24px 100px;
		}

		.story-text p {
			font-size: 19px;
		}


		.facts {
			padding: 60px 24px 90px;
		}

		.fact-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.fact:nth-child(odd),
		.fact:nth-child(even) {
			padding: 28px 0;
		}

		.fact p {
			font-size: 25px;
		}


		.contact {
			padding: 70px 24px 100px;
		}

		.contact h2 {
			font-size: 44px;
		}
	}

</style>
